{"name":"Barrel Stove","hex":"#8e7e67","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"},{"term":"stove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heater, a closed apparatus to burn fuel for the warming of a room.","A device for heating food,  a cooker."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To heat or dry, as in a stove.","To keep warm, in a house or room, by artificial heat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barrel barbecue","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel barbecue is a type of barbecue stove made from a 55-gallon drum barrel. Vents are cut into the top and bottom for airflow control. A lid is used to retain heat. A chimney is not needed because the length of the barrel acts as its own chimney and provides a draft. Short horseshoe-like legs are attached for stability."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel_barbecue","wikidata":"Q4863328"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"},{"title":"Stove","blocks":[{"text":"A stove or range is a device that generates heat inside or atop the device for local heating or cooking. Stoves can be powered with many fuels, such as natural gas, electricity, gasoline, wood, and coal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Indonesian_brick_stove.jpg/330px-Indonesian_brick_stove.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stove","wikidata":"Q203789"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Barrel_barbecue.jpg/120px-Barrel_barbecue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Barrel_barbecue.jpg/250px-Barrel_barbecue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Barrel_barbecue.jpg/120px-Barrel_barbecue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrel_barbecue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg/120px-Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg/250px-Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg/120px-Barrel_barbecue_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrel_barbecue_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w